{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_km7bpxv6y7eozo6co7g2spwivlyriob7zg5d3wxfhorw7kcs6rwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. The Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte across all 45 differential tests × 4 configurations.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` parity | ✅ 5/5 C symbols exported by Rust; 0 missing; 0 undefined non-libc |\n| Phase B — every `CONFIGS.md` row (32) | ✅ 26 tests, randomized w/ fixed seeds |\n| Binary stdout comparison | N/A — no `add_executable`, no `[[bin]]` |\n| Phase C — every `ERRORS.md` row (18 + 5 generic) | ✅ 19 tests |\n| All feature combos | ✅ `default`/`--no-default-features` × `debug`/`release` |\n\n## The one real finding\n\nThe C's `betagamma`/`compute_hash` **compare raw heap addresses** (`mb1->data < mb2->data`, `mb1 < mb2`), so their return values depend on allocator history, not just arguments. Naively loading both `.so`s into one process made every `betagamma` differ by exactly ±10: whichever library ran second popped the chunks the first had just freed off glibc's LIFO tcache and saw the opposite pointer ordering.\n\nThat's a harness artifact, not a translation defect. Fix: an out-of-process oracle (`tests/common/oracle.rs`) that re-executes the test binary twice, dlopening **both** libraries in **both** children (identical heap history) but calling only one. All 10 address-dependent rows then passed unchanged — the Rust code needed no fix. A line-count assertion guards against a vacuous empty-vs-empty pass, and the harness's ability to detect divergence is proven by the ±10 failures it originally caught.\n\n## Correction to my own tables\n\nI initially wrote that `param1 % 10 ∈ {-9..-5}` takes the error path. Wrong: `block_size = (param1%10)+5`, so `-5` yields `block_size == 0`, and `calloc(0,4)` **succeeds**. Only `{-9..-6}` errors. `CONFIGS.md` C18/C19 and `ERRORS.md` E8/E9 were corrected, and `-5` is now an explicit near-miss row.\n\n## Artifacts\n\n`SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `verify.sh` (Phase D driver — enumerates features from `Cargo.toml`, checks symbol diff, runs all combos), `tests/{common/mod.rs,common/oracle.rs,phase_b_valid.rs,phase_c_errors.rs}`. Only change to non-test code: `libloading` added to `[dev-dependencies]`. `src/lib.rs` and `c_src/` are unmodified.\n\nTwo caveats worth flagging: cargo needed `--offline` (crates.io is blocked by the proxy; `libloading 0.8.9` was already cached), and the C is compiled at the CMakeLists' default `-O0` — I did not test whether `-O2` changes the C's behavior on the signed-overflow paths (`sum1 += ...`, `flag_contribution * id`), which are UB and could legally differ between optimization levels."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1017,"cache_read_input_tokens":122467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1017,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"425fa0a8-ee71-4fe0-b59e-ddf257611f7b","uuid":"ff286eea-9034-4f38-af99-aa83925a747c","timestamp":"2026-09-05T13:27:10.747Z"}
